A leading null field is the first element
(2,1)	7
(NULL,1)	7
(NULL,NULL)	7
A nested tuple element is one field
((0,0),1)	7
A multi-character field delimiter keeps the tuple inside one field
(NULL,0)	7
Nullable(Tuple) is still read from a single field
\N	7
The whole-column short-circuit is restored by the opt-out setting
(NULL,0)	1
Regexp reads a tuple inside one capture group
(NULL,1)	7
A capture holding only the null field is short by the remaining elements, as in CSV
